{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:41:30.551Z","data":{"text":"The task is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Added a typed `Manifest` (plus `ApprovalFlags` and `Notices`) deserialized with camelCase serde names, ignoring unknown keys, with every top-level field optional.\n- `read_manifest` now returns `Result<Option<Manifest>, StorageError>`: missing → `Ok(None)`, unreadable → `StorageError::Read`, invalid text/shape/type → new `StorageError::Manifest` whose `Display` starts with the manifest path and whose `source()` is the serde error.\n- `approved_at`, `read_planner` and `manifest_notices` now consume `Option<&Manifest>`; `read_change` propagates with `?`.\n- Added `serde.workspace = true`; `Cargo.lock` changed only in storage's dependency list.\n- Added `tests/reading_manifest.rs` covering all eight table rows in rust-storage \"Manifest files read or refused\", including the `source()` check.\n\nVerification passed: task verify (`cargo test -p osq-kernel-storage --test reading_manifest`) and proposal verify (`sh scripts/verify-rust.sh`, exit 0, corpus tests included)."}}
